{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_23fab6d43c64532d\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_23fab6d43c64532d/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"LT review submission confirmation\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_b94dee3ae64a8b2329242893\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the review never receives a submission confirmation after the tutor scored the recording. Verbatim quote: \\\"Scored the recording, but the review never receives a submission confirmation.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the interface shows a saved/submitted receipt or the same task again in the tutor's thread. Verbatim quote: \\\"Does the interface show a saved/submitted receipt or just the same task again?\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current project instructions require checking the actual receipt before recording submission as complete when confirmation is delayed; a selected rating or successful reload is not proof that the original task was submitted. Verbatim quote: \\\"A selected rating or successful reload is not proof that the original task was submitted.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:3a08035c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided thread contains no answer to the QA tutor's receipt question and does not establish whether the tutor's submission succeeded.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports receiving no submission confirmation after scoring a recording; the thread does not establish whether submission succeeded.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance requires checking the actual receipt before recording submission as complete; selecting a rating is not proof of submission.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:3a08035c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the interface shows a saved/submitted receipt or the same task again; no answer appears in the provided thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Reply in the tutor's thread with the receipt-check rule and ask the tutor to answer the QA tutor's question. Draft to copy: Please check the actual receipt before recording this submission as complete. Selecting a rating or successfully reloading does not prove that the original task was submitted. To answer the QA tutor's question, please clarify what the interface shows: a saved/submitted receipt, or the same task again? That distinction is still missing from this thread, so we cannot yet tell whether the submission succeeded. Scope: Apply this reply to the reported submission-confirmation issue; it does not establish a cause or authorize a workaround.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:3a08035c\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current instructions directly address delayed confirmation. A focused reply applies that rule without treating the missing confirmation as proof of a failed submission.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:3a08035c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): A tutor reports missing submission confirmation, leaving completion unverified while the QA tutor's receipt question remains unanswered.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b94dee3ae64a8b2329242893\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b94dee3ae64a8b2329242893 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor reports no confirmation, and the only follow-up is a QA tutor's unanswered question about the receipt or repeated task display.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: One tutor reports missing confirmation after scoring a recording. The thread does not show inability to complete work, multiple affected tasks, or broader disruption; the immediate correction is to verify the receipt.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U010\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U010 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923021.000115\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b94dee3ae64a8b2329242893\", \"thread_id\": \"1790923021.000115\", \"author_id\": \"U010\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T06:37:01.000115Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U010\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"eyes\", \"users\": [\"U006\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"Scored the recording, but the review never receives a submission confirmation.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790923077.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b94dee3ae64a8b2329242893\", \"thread_id\": \"1790923021.000115\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T06:37:57.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U010\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Does the interface show a saved/submitted receipt or just the same task again?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:3a08035c\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Tool incidents and submission\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Tool incidents and submission\\n| Incident | Required handling |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Playback unavailable | Report task ID and reproduction details; leave content quality unassessed |\\n| Intermittent playback | Record the affected tasks and whether access returned; do not assume every task recovered |\\n| Submit disabled or click fails | Capture task ID, required-field state, error and button behavior |\\n| Confirmation delayed | Check the actual receipt before recording submission as complete |\\n\\nTool incidents are assessed separately under the operational severity rubric. A selected rating or successful reload is not proof that the original task was submitted.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-repeat-observation-review@1.0:ae0550d0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-repeat-observation-review@1.0\", \"title\": \"Repeated ending retained as an observation\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence\", \"Suggested advice\", \"TL decision\", \"State\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-repeat-observation-review\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-29T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-29T14:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_deferred\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_deferred\", \"execution_status\": \"evidence_requested\", \"outcome_status\": \"undetermined\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_deferred; execution_status: evidence_requested; outcome_status: undetermined) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# Repeated ending retained as an observation\\n\\n## Evidence\\nA06-REP-14 was reported as speaking the last phrase twice although its transcript showed the phrase once. The review packet contained a player screenshot and the transcript, but no downloaded recording or comparison on a second player.\\n\\n## Suggested advice\\nA simulated Advisor card proposed escalating a confirmed audio-generation loop.\\n\\n## TL decision\\nPriya deferred that claim and retained the report as a model/process observation. Request a downloaded-file versus player comparison when available. A repeated phrase in the player does not yet locate the defect in the generated file.\\n\\nNo FAQ rule change or confirmed model-defect announcement was approved. If the additional evidence establishes a generation defect or material operational impact, reassess the intervention.\\n\\n## State\\nThe observation is open. There is no completed diagnostic comparison or engineering escalation in this record.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-playback-trial-outcome@1.0:16332fce\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-playback-trial-outcome@1.0\", \"title\": \"Playback trial follow-up — unsuitable as a general workaround\", \"sections\": [\"Trial observation\", \"TL conclusion\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-playback-trial-outcome\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"follow_up\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-27T16:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-27T16:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_05\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"reported\", \"decision_status\": \"reported\", \"execution_status\": \"trial_completed\", \"outcome_status\": \"unsuccessful_in_sample\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (follow_up; decision_status: reported; execution_status: trial_completed; outcome_status: unsuccessful_in_sample) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Trial observation\\nPriya reviewed the six reported trial attempts below. Each row records the participant's observed result after one reload; the review did not establish a common underlying cause.\\n\\n| Task | Playback after one reload |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| A05-P101 | Started |\\n| A05-P102 | Still stuck |\\n| A05-P103 | Still stuck |\\n| A05-P104 | Started |\\n| A05-P105 | Still stuck |\\n| A05-P106 | Still stuck |\\n\\n## TL conclusion\\nTwo of six attempts restored playback; four did not. The trial did not provide a dependable general workaround. The batch-05 authorization remains time-limited and is not extended into a later queue.\\n\\nContinue recording task IDs and reproduction details. Do not describe the incident as fixed or assume that a new batch has the same cause.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-headset-check-approval@1.0:3741e593\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-headset-check-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"Approve a workstation output check for two silent-listening reports\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-headset-check-approval\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-21T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-21T14:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nMina's intake notes identify two affected tasks, A06-H031 and A06-H032, on WS-A03. In both observations the player counter advanced from 00:00 to 00:12 while the tutor heard nothing. A known-good reference clip was also inaudible on that workstation. Mina heard the reference clip on WS-A04; neither affected task had yet been checked there.\\n\\nNo browser error, frozen counter, or unavailable waveform was recorded. The evidence supports checking the listening setup, but does not establish a silent source recording or a repaired task.\\n\\nAt the review cutoff, no output-device change or successful replay of the affected tasks had been recorded. The approved diagnostic is pending.\\n\\n## Prior ThreadSense advice\\n\\nAsk the two affected tutors to check the selected output device and headset connection, then replay a known-good reference and their original tasks. Keep content quality unassessed until audible playback is verified.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"HISTORY_ONLY\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-playback-trial-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Playback trial posted to audio announcements\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1787581200.700001\